<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_Greatbole.xml                                   GREENTIDE_JUNGLE_TREE_ROSTER_1

  The signature giant — design doc §3a0, row 22. Ruled 2026-09-22: the
  LANDMARK (RUT_GreatboleCore/RUT_GreatboleHeartwood, campaign-tier,
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards + UtinniPatches, unfellable) and this
  FELLABLE giant are the SAME SPECIES at different life stages — the
  landmark is what a greatbole becomes after centuries, this is the mature
  tree a player actually fells. They share a visual family (leaf, bark
  plating, fluting — never a silhouette, since one is a tree and the other
  is a mineable cross-section too vast to draw as one) and NOTHING ELSE:
  no shared def, no shared comp, no growth path between them (his own
  ruling: "the game will not actually simulate that growth ... the
  relationship is fiction, and the description carrying it IS the
  implementation" — do not build one).

  This def was explicitly OWED by three other closed items before this pass:
  RM_GreatboleHarvest_Items.xml's own header ("checked this pass, that def
  does not exist anywhere in src/ yet"), GREATBOLE_HARVEST_LADDER_1's own
  Watch-out ("say which greatbole def you mean"), and this mod's own
  About.xml ("a franchise-free source ... is owed separately"). It retires
  RUT_Placeholder_GreentideGiantTree.xml, the mechanism-proof stub that
  existed only so RM_TreeFallUtility/RM_CompCrackFall/RM_FellableTreeExtension
  were provably wired end-to-end — this is the real roster giant that
  placeholder's own header said would eventually replace it.

  Tier: RM_ (franchise-free), per the 2026-09-22 "no canon trees" ruling —
  "greatbole" is existing project vocabulary (MEASURED in 20 files under
  src/, checked again for this defName specifically: zero collisions) but is
  not itself Star Wars IP, so nothing about it needs to live behind the
  campaign layer. This closes the tier gap the design doc flagged as "not
  mine to decide": the free mod now gets its OWN mature giant (this def)
  rather than only ever meeting the campaign-tier landmark it can never
  encounter.

  Interface with the harvest-ladder work (GREATBOLE_HARVEST_LADDER_1): this
  def does NOT carry RUT_CompGreatboleHarvestLadder — that comp is the
  LANDMARK's own threshold ladder (40/60/70% mined-away events) and is
  Utinni/RUT_ tier by construction (its own header: "attach this alongside
  ... on RUT_GreatboleCore"), unreachable from an RM_ tier def without
  crossing the tier line. This tree's own "interface" with that work is
  fictional continuity only (same species) plus the ALREADY-GENERIC
  mechanism the harvest-ladder item itself relies on and that this roster
  was built to finally give real content: RM_FellableTreeExtension +
  RM_TreeFallUtility.FellTree (RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards,
  def-agnostic, MEASURED by RM_TreeFallUtility.cs:67's own
  GetModExtension<RM_FellableTreeExtension>() ?? Default fallback). Setting
  isGiantClass=true here is what GREATBOLE_HARVEST_LADDER_1's own design doc
  §4a calls "what closes Q1" (true hardwood by felling).

  hardwoodDef points at RM_GreatboleHardwood (RM_Greentide_TreeRoster_Items.
  xml), a NEW RM-tier parallel to the campaign-tier RUT_Hardwood — not a
  reference to RUT_Hardwood itself, which would make this RM_ tier def
  depend on the Utinni campaign patch layer. Same "duplicate rather than
  cross-reference" posture the 2026-09-23 biome-mod-split rulings already
  established for shared content between an RM_ mod and its campaign twin.

  Art: OWED, and the largest canvas on the roster page (2048x2048 at the
  128px/cell canvas law, 16 cells) — no existing artpipe subject matches a
  colossal fluted-column-under-a-leaf-raft giant tree (checked
  infrastructure/artpipe/done/, _artsrc/, registry.jsonl this pass, per §3f
  of the design doc; the four transferable subjects all key to ordinary
  canopy/mid rows, not the giant). Placeholder texPath points at the owed
  location; do not deploy against a donor texture — this tree's whole
  narrative point is that it visually announces the landmark it will
  become, which no existing art was built to do.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">
    <defName>RM_Greatbole</defName>
    <label>greatbole</label>
    <description>A single grey-brown column so broad at the base that its fluting reads as separate trunks fused together, rising far past every other crown before opening into one horizontal raft of paddle leaves. Bark in long vertical plates that shed. Nothing grows in its shadow, so it stands in a clearing of its own making. Given centuries and left uncut, a greatbole like this one becomes something else entirely — a trunk too vast to still be called a tree.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- OWED, largest canvas on the page (2048x2048, 16 cells). See header. -->
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Greatbole/RM_Greatbole_a</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(0.8, 1.1, 0.6)</volume>
        <offset>(0,0,-0.6)</offset>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>1400</MaxHitPoints>
      <!-- "Very low", the roster-wide fire ruling — lower even than the
           ordinary trees' neighbourhood, matching a trunk too wet and too
           vast to readily burn at all. -->
      <Flammability>0.05</Flammability>
      <Nutrition>3.0</Nutrition>
      <Mass>3000</Mass>
      <BeautyOutdoors>6</BeautyOutdoors>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <!-- "Well past 10" per the owner's own ruling on where the boldness
           goes (above the range, not into the mid-storey). Veluthar (10) is
           the largest ordinary canopy tree; 16 puts this ~60% past it. -->
      <growDays>220</growDays>
      <harvestWork>10000</harvestWork>
      <harvestYield>150</harvestYield>
      <visualSizeRange>12.0~16.0</visualSizeRange>
      <!-- Rare and solitary by design — the signature specimen, not a
           common canopy tree. Wide radius, very low weight. -->
      <wildClusterRadius>14</wildClusterRadius>
      <wildClusterWeight>1.5</wildClusterWeight>
      <treeLoversCareIfChopped>true</treeLoversCareIfChopped>
    </plant>
    <modExtensions>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards" Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_FellableTreeExtension">
        <isGiantClass>true</isGiantClass>
        <fellLength>16</fellLength>
        <fallDamageRange>150~260</fallDamageRange>
        <heartRadius>2</heartRadius>
        <hardwoodDropRange>8~14</hardwoodDropRange>
        <greenwoodStackRange>30~60</greenwoodStackRange>
        <greenwoodDropChancePerCell>0.8</greenwoodDropChancePerCell>
        <greenwoodDef>WoodLog</greenwoodDef>
        <hardwoodDef>RM_GreatboleHardwood</hardwoodDef>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
